<title>USA: Freddie Mac sets $250 mln in REMIC 1935.</title>
<headline>Freddie Mac sets $250 mln in REMIC 1935.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp (Freddie Mac or FHLMC) said it issued $250 million of Real Estate Mortgage Investment Conduit (REMIC) securities.</p>
<p>REMIC series 1935, underwritten by Credit Suisse First Boston  CSHZn.S, has a coupon of 8.0 percent and is backed by 30-year single-family fixed-rate mortgages, Freddie Mac said. It priced January 27 and has a settlement date of February 28. The issue has a weighted average maturity of 349 months, a weigthed average coupon of 8.60 percent and a weighted average loan age of 11, the agency said.</p>
<p>(( -- Jeff Coelho, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
